;; spec:   stdlib §4.4 row realized? (an adaptor has no cell and is a compile error), §2.1 rule 2
;; expect: reject
;; error:  cannot unify (Mapped (Vec i64) i64 i64) with (LSeq a)
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: realized?
;; realized? asks an LSeq whether its first node has been computed. A recipe is built without a
;; cell, never a value of a program, and holds no flag, so the question has no answer and the program
;; is refused: the argument must be an LSeq, and the message says what it was given.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq))

(defun main () -> i64
  (if (realized? (Mapped [1 2] (fn (x: i64) x))) 1 0))
